          <register>
            <name>APPLYPARAMETERSA</name>
            <description>SCP APPLY PARAMETERS A</description>
            <addressOffset>0x1B8</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>APPLYPARAMETERSA</name>
                <description>If the SYNCHRONISE_UPDATES bit is set in the Control register, a number of parameters are updated synchronously when the sample number is equal to (APPLY_PARAMETERS_A - 1). Thus, with the control bit set, writes to the parameter fields are held off until SAMPLE_NUMBER_A = (APPLY_PARAMETERS_A - 1). If SYNCHRONISE_UPDATES is not set, updates to the parameters occur immediately that they are written to the appropriate registers.The following parameter updates are synchronized:- GAIN_CONTROL_1- GAIN_CONTROL_2- OFFSET_CONTROL_1- OFFSET_CONTROL_2- DC_OFFSET_I- DC_OFFSET_Q- COARSE_GAIN- I_GAIN- Q_GAIN- I_TO_Q_GAIN- FS- FC</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
