                <name>IQIMBALANCEBYPASS</name>
                <description>Used to set the bypass mode of the IQ imbalance compensation block:</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>IqImbalanceCompensat</name>
                    <description>IQ imbalance compensation is active.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>IqImbalanceCompensta</name>
                    <description>IQ imbalance compenstation block is powered down and data passes around it unaltered.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>DRMDECIMATORCTRL</name>
            <description>SCP DRM DECIMATOR CTRL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x2D8</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>DRMDECRATIO</name>
                <description>Decimation ratio (if DRM_DEC_EN is set):0: Decimate by 1 (no decimation)1: Decimate by 215: Decimate by 16</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DRMDECEN</name>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>12</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>BypassDrmDecimator</name>
                    <description>Bypass DRM decimator</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>EnableDecimation</name>
                    <description>Enable decimation</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <cluster>
            <dim>8</dim>
            <dimIncrement>0x00C</dimIncrement>
            <name>EARLYGAINLUT[%s]</name>
            <description>Unspecified</description>
            <headerStructName>WIFIPHY_SCP_EARLYGAINLUT</headerStructName>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <addressOffset>0x2E0</addressOffset>
            <register>
              <name>EARLYFINEGAINI</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP EARLY FINE GAIN I</description>
              <addressOffset>0x000</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00200000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>EARLYIGAIN</name>
                  <description>2's complement value that multiplies I value from SCP.This is a linear gain where 0x800 represents the 0dB point, thus the fine gain is EARLY_I_GAIN/0x800.Bits 23:13 valid for 12-bit SCP, bits 23:10 valid for 16-bit SCP.</description>
                  <lsb>10</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
              <name>EARLYFINEGAINQ</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP EARLY FINE GAIN Q</description>
              <addressOffset>0x004</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00200000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>EARLYQGAIN</name>
                  <description>2's complement value that multiplies Q value from SCP.This is a linear gain where 0x800 represents the 0dB point, thus the fine gain is EARLY_Q_GAIN/0x800.Bits 23:13 valid for 12-bit SCP, bits 23:10 valid for 16-bit SCP.</description>
                  <lsb>10</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
              <name>EARLYANGLEIQ</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP EARLY ANGLE IQ</description>
              <addressOffset>0x008</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>EARLYITOQGAIN</name>
                  <description>2's complement value that multiplies I value before addition to Q value in the early gain block.Qout = Q + (I * EARLY_I_TO_Q_GAIN &amp;gt;&amp;gt; 13).Bits 23:13 valid for 12-bit SCP, bits 23:10 valid for 16-bit SCP.</description>
                  <lsb>10</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
          </cluster>
          <register>
            <name>COREID</name>
            <description>SCP CORE ID</description>
            <addressOffset>0x340</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
            <resetValue>0x000F0200</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>CORECONFIG</name>
                <description>Configuration of the core.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>COREID</name>
                <description>Identifies the member of the IP group.</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>GROUPID</name>
                <description>Identifies core as part of an IMG IP family group.</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>COREREVISION</name>
            <description>SCP CORE REVISION</description>
            <addressOffset>0x350</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
            <resetValue>0x00020000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>MAINTENANCEREV</name>
                <description>Maintenance Release Revision</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>MINORREV</name>
                <description>Core Minor Release Revision</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>MAJORREV</name>
                <description>Family Major Release Revision</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>GNSSOUTPUTFORMAT</name>
            <description>SCP GNSS OUTPUT FORMAT</description>
            <addressOffset>0x360</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>GNSSOUTPUTFORMAT</name>
                <description>SCP, GNSS Location Core output format selection.0:1x I/Q pair(12-bits per component)This represents standard SCP operation.1:3x I/Q pairs(4-bits per component)2:4x I/Q pairs(3-bits per component)3:6x I/Q pairs(2-bits per component)4: 12x I/Q pairs(1-bitper component)Other values are reserved and must not be used.Where a non-zero value is set in this register the 12-bit samples in each pair are reduced to the k-bit width indicated by selecting the k MSBs from each 12-bit sample.Setting this register to a non-zero value assumes TBUS_OUTPUT_FORMAT=0</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>2</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>TBUSCONTROL</name>
            <description>SCP TBUS CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x380</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>TBUSOUTPUTFORMAT</name>
                <description>Used to select TBus output format:0 : 12-bit real in upper and 12-bit imaginary in lower 24 bits of TBus output (default).1 : Alternating 16-bit imaginary followed by 16-bit real, left aligned in 24-bits of output TBus.8-bit lsbs are zero padded and full 24 bits transferred to memory by EDC for processing as 24-bit double by MCP.This case is only relevant on 16-bit SCPs.Note reference to this register in the description of register GNSS_OUTPUT_FORMAT.2 : Alternating 16-bit imaginary followed by 16-bit real, right aligned in 24-bits of output TBus.Sign extended to 24 bits but in practice only lower 16 bits will be transferred to memory by EDC for processing as 32-bit complex by MCU.This case is only relevant on 16-bit SCPs.Note reference to this register in the description of register GNSS_OUTPUT_FORMAT.3 : Alternating 12-bit real followed by 12-bit imaginary, where each 12-bit word is left shifted by 4 and signed extended to 24-bits.</description>
                <lsb>18</lsb>
                <msb>19</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>TBUSOUTPUTSTALL</name>
                <description>Used to enable or disable stalling of SCP when output FIFO is full:</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>StallingOfScpDisable</name>
                    <description>Stalling of SCP disabled when output FIFO is full.TBUS_OVERFLOW_EVENT flagged when SCP output overflows TBus output FIFO.OVERFLOW_EVENT can also be flagged when input data rate too high for enabled processing (i.e. due to re-sample factor, or enabling of notch/impulse filters).</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>StallingOfScpEnabled</name>
                    <description>Stalling of SCP enabled when output FIFO is full.TBUS_OVERFLOW_EVENT not flagged, only OVERFLOW_EVENT flagged when input data rate too high for enabled processing (i.e. due to re-sample factor, or enabling of notch/impulse filters), or as a result of EDC TBus job rate being too slow.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
