              <field>
                <name>LGNEXTLNASTAGETABLE46</name>
                <description>The stage index of the next LNA stage to use, if the current lna stage is 4 and rf rssi value is 6.It has a range of 0 .. 7.</description>
                <lsb>18</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGNEXTLNASTAGETABLE47</name>
                <description>The stage index of the next LNA stage to use, if the current lna stage is 4 and rf rssi value is 7.It has a range of 0 .. 7.</description>
                <lsb>21</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANAGCLGCCONFIG10</name>
            <description>WLAN AGC LGC CONFIG 10</description>
            <addressOffset>0x6C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00152F58</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE0</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 0, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LG_RSSI_INCR_POWER_FACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm)'This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -40.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE1</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 1, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LG_RSSI_INCR_POWER_FACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm)'This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -34.</description>
                <lsb>7</lsb>
                <msb>13</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE2</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 2, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LG_RSSI_INCR_POWER_FACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm)'This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -28.</description>
                <lsb>14</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANAGCLGCCONFIG11</name>
